# RESILIENT-1108 (Outcome-Verification, umbrella RESILIENT-1103) — the organ
# that verifies organs actually RAN and SUCCEEDED, not merely that their timer
# is-active. Runs one pass of scripts/ops/organ-success-verifier.sh, which reads
# each manifest-`enabled` organ's last-run systemctl Result/ExecMainStatus and
# pages the duty officer on any FAILED run (200/CHDIR, non-zero exit, etc.).
#
# WHY THIS UNIT ITSELF AVOIDS A WorkingDirectory. The all-night incident this
# organ exists to catch was caused by a WorkingDirectory=/home/ubuntu/Projects/
# chump that did not exist on the node — systemd killed every organ at chdir(2)
# (status=200/CHDIR) before ExecStart ran. So this unit sets NO WorkingDirectory
# at all and instead invokes the script by absolute path, exactly like
# chump-organ-watchdog.service and chump-outcome-verify-heal-consumer.service.
#
# Host-agnostic via the systemd /root specifier (INFRA-3647): install-helsinki-
# atc.sh inserts the per-node User= line at deploy time, so /root resolves to
# root's home on helsinki and to the run-user's home on an owned node from this
# SAME tracked unit. CHUMP_REPO_ROOT is REQUIRED because the script's default
# $HOME/Projects/Chump is capital-C and does not exist on case-sensitive Linux.
[Unit]
Description=Chump organ-success verifier — page on any organ whose last run FAILED (RESILIENT-1108)
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=root
Environment=HOME=/root
Environment=CHUMP_REPO_ROOT=/root/Projects/chump
ExecStart=/bin/bash -lc 'set -a; source /root/.chump/providers.env 2>/dev/null; set +a; exec /root/Projects/chump/scripts/ops/organ-success-verifier.sh'
